# Firebase sync notes for admission + kit fee rollout

- New per-class **kit charges** now live under the `settings/general` document in Firestore (field: `kitCharges`).
  - Update those amounts in the accountant portal Settings tab to feed the admission manager’s payment calculations.
  - Default map is the Nursery–Class 9 set already shown in the UI; values are read directly by admission-manager.
- Admission records created from the admission manager now carry additional fields for approval and dues tracking:
  - `admissionFeeAmount`, `kitChargeAmount`, `totalAmountDue`, `amountPaid`, `balanceAmount`, `paymentPlan`, and `remainingInstallments`.
  - Payments created for admissions also store `total_amount`, `balance_after`, `payment_plan`, `admission_amount`, and `kit_amount`.
- No Firebase config or security rule changes are required at this time; existing authenticated read/write rules already cover the new fields and collections.
